{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Can Defect Tracking Have Negative Implications?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about defect tracking. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in written and spoken situations and in work and social contexts. Train the system users on application structuring and management, according to the established plan and user profile, according to the organization policies."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  Recognizes simple ideas on managing a proposed application, using available hardware for an application, and technical reports on an IT solution."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Must Have, May Have, Might Have, and Could Have for Speculating About the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs for speculating about the past</span> when we want to explain or draw conclusions about an event in the past. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When we are not sure about how a past event took place, we can speculate by using modal verbs. The basic structure for this, is the following:<br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <span class=\"strong\">modal verb + have + past participle of main verb</span> + complement</div><br/><br/>  Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">The defect fixing process <span class=\"strong\">could have been</span> much more effective. </span><br/><br/>  We can also use these <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs</span> in the negative form. The structure for this would be the following:<br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <span class=\"strong\">modal verb + not + have + past participle of main verb</span> + complement</div><br/><br/>  Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">The defect fixing process <span class=\"strong\">should not have been</span> so tedious. </span><br/><br/>  There are different modal verbs we can use for providing more information about how certain we are about the past event. Let's take a look at the following chart:<br/>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Level of certainty</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Did happen</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Did not happen</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">very certain</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Must have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">must have</span> tracked defects. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Must not have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">must not have</span> tracked defects. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">kind of certain</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could have</span> tracked less defects. </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could not have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could not have</span> tracked defects. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">not very certain</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"May have</br></br>Might have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">may have</span> solved the defects. </span></br></br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">might have</span> solved the defects. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"May not have </br></br> Might not have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">may not have</span> solved the defects.</br></br> We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">might not have</span> solved the defects.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "They must have wasted a lot of time entering the information about these defects since this process can be time-demanding. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They may have misunderstood the real function of this system, which is to facilitate work and not to demand the team to enter every possible piece of information about all the bugs they find."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They might not have realized that tracking bugs that aren't going to get fixed is harmful for the process, since this is a waste of time for the team."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The company might have disregarded the advantages of direct communication, in which both developers and testers can discuss face to face and clear up any misunderstandings."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Notice that in the negative form, the modal verb <span class=\"strong\">\u2018could'</span> has a high level of certainty and the modal verbs <span class=\"strong\">\u2018may'</span> and <span class=\"strong\">\u2018might'</span> can express a middle or a low level of certainty in the negative form.  "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Bug/Defect Tracking Systems"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A bug tracking system, also known as a defect tracking system, is a software application whose function is to keep track of bugs in software development projects.   <br/><br/>  A bug tracking system is usually a very important part of a good software development project as it allows the team to evaluate defects and make sure they do not pass unnoticed.   <br/><br/>  The bug tracking system uses a database that records the important facts about the known bugs. These facts can include the time at which the bug was reported, how severe it is, why it is a defect, and who is in charge of fixing it. By using this system, the team will have clear information and an overview of the defects found in the development process of a product. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "detrimental "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is harmful"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Defect metrics can be detrimental if they are used for measuring the tester's productivity."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "due to the fact that "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "as a consequence of, for this reason"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I felt tension between some of the members, and this may have been due to the fact that a report is a poor means of communication and both parties can feel their work is being underestimated by the other."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "disregard"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to neglect or pay no attention to something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The company might have disregarded the advantages of direct communication, in which both developers and testers can discuss face to face and clear up any misunderstandings."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "underestimated"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is not estimated for the value it deserves"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I felt tension between some of the members, and this may have been due to the fact that a report is a means of poor communication and both parties can feel their work is being underestimated by the other."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "whereas"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "on the contrary, while"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(connector)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The company could have disregarded the advantages of direct communication in which both developers and testers can discuss face to face and clear up any misunderstandings, whereas, defect tracking can sometimes mislead to a wrong interpretation of one another's words.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mislead "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to lead towards a wrong direction or conclusion"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Defect tracking can sometimes mislead to a wrong interpretation of one another's words."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read about tracking defects system."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe how  it works."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a brochure about that system."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Show your brochure to your classmates and teacher."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about tracking defects system."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe how  it works."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a brochure."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I show my brochure to my classmates and teacher."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can explain what a bug or defect tracking system is."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can explain what a bug or defect tracking system is."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about why defect tracking metrics can become detrimental."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Have you ever had any problems with defect tracking processes? What were they?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "When do you think defect tracking can be counterproductive?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type"